### tinybendygrad/codegen/decomp/dtype.bend  (3072 lines)
    1| # dtype.bend -- tinygrad/codegen/decomp/dtype.py (224 lines).
    2| #
    3| # THE LONG AND FLOAT DECOMPOSITIONS. `dtype.py` splits a 64-bit or an
    4| # fp8/half/bfloat16 arithmetic node into 32-bit words (`l2i`) or into a
    5| # bit-level float conversion (`f2f`), and rewrites the graph so the 32-bit nodes
    6| # reach the hardware. This file is the SPLIT half -- `l2i`, `f2f`, `f2f_clamp`,
    7| # `reindex`, `unpack32`, `rne`, `l2i_define` and the three pattern tables --
    8| # which is most of the 224 lines. The REWRITE half (`split_l2i`,
    9| # `l2i_rewrite_idx`, `f2f_load`, `f2f_store`, `f2f_rewrite`,
   10| # `do_dtype_decomps`) is PORTED IN SHAPE, and each def says so.
   11| #
   12| # `decomp/op.bend` is the sibling (`decomp/op.py`) and
   13| # `decomp/transcendental.bend` is the other half of `decomp/transcendental.py`.
   14| # BOTH ARE IMPORTED, not re-derived: `P.dc_*` is `op.bend`'s node vocabulary
   15| # (its `dc_sub` IS `__sub__`'s shape, its `dc_band` IS `x & k`, its `dc_cint` IS
   16| # `UOp.const(v)`) and `T.tx_*` / `T.exponent_bias` / `T.tx_is_fnuz` /
   17| # `T.tx_finfo_*` is `transcendental.bend`'s. `dtype.py` itself imports
   18| # `exponent_bias`, `shl` and `shr` FROM `transcendental.py`, so those three are
   19| # used under `transcendental.bend`'s names and are not re-derived here.
   20| #
   21| # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   22| # THE INVENTORY, def by def, against dtype.py's 224 lines.
   23| #
   24| #   #  PY        KIND    STATE
   25| #   1  12        data    l2i_dt                     PORTED IN FULL
   26| #   2  13        graph   unpack32                   PORTED IN FULL
   27| #   3  14-18     graph   reindex                    PORTED IN FULL
   28| #   4  21-81     graph   l2i                        15 of 17 arms, every arm shape
   29| #   5  83-86     graph   l2i_define                 PORTED IN FULL
   30| #   6  88-92     rewrite split_l2i                 PORTED IN SHAPE
  ... cited lines ...
     97| # `f2f_clamp` mints `mx` with `val.const_like(...)` and `val` is `v.bitcast(fr)`,
     98| # so `mx` is a CONST at the SOURCE's width: CPython truncates it with
>>   99| # `float_to_fp16` / `float_to_bf16` / `float_to_fp8` (`dtype.py:225/229/244`,
    100| # all `struct` and bit-twiddling C code) and this file has none of them. THE
      ROW: subj=dtype.py 225-225 class=ambient_relocated tokens=float_to_fp16,float_to_bf16,float_to_fp8

