### tinybendygrad/codegen/decomp/transcendental.bend  (2028 lines)
    1| # transcendental.bend -- tinygrad/codegen/decomp/transcendental.py (277 lines).
    2| #
    3| # THE GRAPH HALF.  `tinybendygrad/codegen/transcendental_f32.bend` ports the OTHER
    4| # half of these same 277 lines -- the COEFFICIENTS and the float32 VALUES -- and
    5| # the two are complementary, not duplicates.  Both headers state the split; read
    6| # that one for why they are not merged (two oracles, and a 0.17 s coefficient lane
    7| # against a 21 min value lane).  Neither file imports the other.
    8| #
    9| # THE SOFTWARE TRANSCENDENTAL EXPANSIONS: `exp2`/`log2`/`sin`/`sqrt` as
   10| # polynomial-plus-bit-trick trees, and the seven-entry pattern table that fires
   11| # them. `decomp.bend` is the sibling (`decomp/op.py`); its header says so and it
   12| # carries NONE of this.
   13| #
   14| # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   15| # THE INVENTORY, def by def, against transcendental.py's 277 lines. Python's
   16| # order is kept; two blocks move and each says why.
   17| #
   18| #   #  PY        KIND    STATE
