### tinybendygrad/engine/jit.bend  (435 lines)
    1| # jit.bend -- tinygrad/engine/jit.py:180 symbol=TinyJit. `TinyJit`: the input spec, the run counter, the
    2| # `captured` record and the dispatch that decides, on every call, whether to EAGERLY RUN, to
    3| # CAPTURE, or to REPLAY.
    4| #
    5| # THE SIBLING THAT OWNS MY TYPES. `tinybendygrad/function.bend` is porting
    6| # `tinygrad/function.py`, which is where the OTHER decorator lives. NOTHING FROM THAT FILE IS
    7| # RE-PORTED HERE, and the reason is a fact about the PYTHON rather than about taste:
    8| # `engine/jit.py`'s `TinyJit` and `function.py`'s `_function` are two different wrappers on
    9| # two different hooks. `_function` rewrites a traced graph into a `CALL`; `TinyJit` captures
   10| # LINEARs produced by `capturing` and replays them. Measured:
   11| #     rg -n "JitMatchError|input_spec|assigned_vars" tinygrad/   -> no hits
   12| #     rg -n "class TinyJit"    tinygrad/                         -> engine/jit.py:104
   13| #     rg -n "class _function"  tinygrad/                         -> function.py:39
   14| # So the unit brief's "input spec / count / misc / vars / JitMatchError" are from an OLDER
   15| # `engine/jit.py`. THIS checkout's match is
   16| # `self.captured.expected_input_info != expected_input_info` (jit.py:173), the counter is
   17| # `self.cnt` (jit.py:107), the error is `JitError` (jit.py:44), and the gate below is built
   18| # against THIS file's messages, byte for byte, against CPython.
   19| # `examples/beautiful_mnist.ts` (committed) reimplements the same idea in TypeScript with a
   20| # SHAPE string and a DIFFERENT message -- `train_step was captured with 1568/2 and called with
   21| # 1568/3` -- and that difference is itself a measured finding: see `ref_shape_drift` in
   22| # Section 11. WHAT I EXPECT `function.bend` TO EXPORT, so the merge is mechanical: NOTHING.
   23| # `function.py` imports nothing from `engine/jit.py`; the dependency runs the other way. If
   24| # `function.bend` ever wants the `@TinyJit` decorator it needs `tiny_jit.of3(f)` /
   25| # `tiny_jit.of2(prune, f)` from Section 9, and those take a function VALUE, so the two files
   26| # compose without a cycle.
   27| #
   28| # WHAT IS PORTED, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE LIST.
   29| #   jit.py:14-22   prune_linear            the fold, `needed |= si_bufs`, both replaces
   30| #   jit.py:24-27   _copy_input             the DISK refusal and `on_disk()`
  ... cited lines ...
     33| #   jit.py:42-47   _check_no_non_tensor_return   the walk and its message
     34| #   jit.py:34-43 symbol=linear   CapturedJit fields, `linear`
>>   35| #   jit.py:62-64   _written_uops           PORTED, via realize.bend's `get_call_written_bufs`
     36| #   jit.py:71-73   _symbolic_ret           the comprehension; `get_parameters` is a seam
      ROW: subj=jit.py 62-64 class=only_older_revision tokens=get_call_written_bufs

