### tinybendygrad/schedule/multi.bend  (3456 lines)
    1| # multi.bend -- tinygrad/schedule/multi.py. Multi-device scheduling: the UNSHARD-splitting
    2| # rules, the device-group COPY rules, and the MSELECT/MSTACK rewrites.
    3| #
    4| # WHAT THIS FILE IS. `multi.py` is 311 lines and THIRTY defs, and almost none of it is
    5| # arithmetic. Two thirds of the defs are GRAPH BUILDERS (`.unshard`, `.alu`, `.mselect`,
    6| # `.copy_to_device`, `._shard`, `.cat`, `.store`, `.replace`, `UOp(Ops.STACK, ...)`) and not
    7| # one of those is ported (ops.py:423 through :32, every one a `TODO(p3)` in `ops.bend`).
    8| # What IS here is the DECISION and the INDEX ARITHMETIC each of those thirty defs makes
    9| # before it reaches for a builder -- which axes a REDUCE consumes, where a RESHAPE's shard
   10| # boundary lands, which axis a PERMUTE sends a shard to and which it FLIPs, whether a
   11| # shrink resolves its own UNSHARD, whether an INDEX is contiguously or strided owned, and
   12| # the three-way per-source decision in `shard_srcs` that the resharding fallbacks all call.
   13| #
   14| # THE ONE WALL THAT CUTS ACROSS EVERY LINE: `UOp._min_max` (ops.py:1094), which
   15| # `int(rng.vmax)+1` needs in `shard_srcs`, `shrink_multi`, `reshape_multi` and
   16| # `copy_multi`. `fold.bend` names it `ops.py:1104` in its own PROSE and carries it as
   17| # its `_min_max` WALK -- there is no `TODO(p3)` marker for it there -- and it is not a
   18| # fold at all -- it is arithmetic over the srcs. What `mu_count`
   19| # ports is the NARROW case that is exact and load-bearing: a RANGE over a CONST end, where
   20| # ops.py:1137 reads `(self.src[0]-1).vmax` so `int(rng.vmax)+1 == src[0]`, which is exactly
