### tinybendygrad/uop/fold.bend  (7393 lines)
    1| # fold.bend -- the derived properties of tinygrad/uop/ops.py, as ONE topological
    2| # fold over the arena.
    3| #
    4| # WHAT THIS FILE IS. `ops.bend` builds the arena: a UOp is a `U32` index into an
    5| # append-only `List<Node>`, so every property read goes through the store. That
    6| # store is what stops the property folds -- a self-call must pass a FIELD of its
    7| # own parameter and the arena's field is a U32 read back out of a store -- and
    8| # mutual recursion is refused, and `dtype_from_uop` <-> `_shape` <->
    9| # `simplify()` -> `graph_rewrite` -> the rules -> `dtype` is a cycle.
   10| #
   11| # THE FIX is the shape `toposort` already has in `ops.bend`: ONE def that walks
   12| # the graph in topological order, so a node is answered only after every node it
   13| # reads is. Python's `recursive_property` (ops.py:211) replaces
   14| # `functools.cached_property` in recursive UOp functions to prevent
   15| # RecursionError; this is the same answer with no recursion at all. The dependency
   16| # graph of the fold is a DAG BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by discipline, and
   17| # `graph_rewrite` is not called, so nothing in the rewrite engine can call back
   18| # into this file.
   19| #
   20| # dtype and shape are answered TOGETHER, as one `DtShape`, because they read each
   21| # other -- `_shape`'s CALL/INS/BITCAST arms read `self.dtype`, and
   22| # `dtype_from_uop`'s INDEX arm reads `b.shape` -- and because a pair is what a
   23| # caller wants. The other properties keep their own `match op`, which is what
   24| # Python has: `device`, `addrspace`, `base` and `ended_ranges` are separate
   25| # properties there and separate defs here. `derived` is the one place they are
   26| # assembled, and it is the only def that knows about all of them.
   27| #
   28| # THE FIVE MOVEMENT ARMS ARE LANDED, and THREE OF THEM WERE NOT BEHIND THE WALL THE
   29| # TODO LIST RECORDED FOR THEM. It said EXPAND, PERMUTE and FLIP wait on
   30| # "`marg` -> `as_shape` -> `ssimplify`", which is TRUE of `marg`'s first two arms and
  ... cited lines ...
    130| #
    131| # THE LATTICE IS HOISTED, with a notice. `promo_dtype` needs `least_upper_dtype`
>>  132| # (dtype.py:193), which `./../dtype.bend` already has in a form this file cannot
